BEGIN_DESC
Io, day side: the heavy suit "Pantsir" (class 2, Orbitersdk/OrbiterCrew/HEAVY_SUIT.md) against the plain "Karkas".
Pantsir: 130 kg (the servos carry it), 4 g/cm2 shield + tantalum liner, a field of up to 2 kW in steps, 20 kWh battery, 2.5 kW supply.
FIELD (top right of the suit computer) steps OFF -> 25 -> 50 -> 75 -> 100 %: watch the dose rate against the battery hours.
Here (Io surface ~1.5 Sv/h): field off ~330 mSv/h; 25 % ~24 mSv/h (28 h); 50 % ~14 mSv/h (16 h); 100 % ~8 mSv/h (8-9 h).
Above ~75 % little is gained: the bremsstrahlung (~3 mSv/h) only the mass and the liner stop.
THERMAL CONTROL panel: "Heat limit" - the hottest surroundings the suit holds with the present loads (it floats: the field is shed
first over the supply, the coils heat the equipment); the evaporator (6 kg of water, up to 1 kW) buys time past it.
Kaira Rean stands beside her in the light "Karkas" with its 600 W field (~23 mSv/h) for comparison.
END_DESC

